1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,353
First... step three, Bima Bharosa, the online complaint portal of the insurance regulator, the I-R-D-A-I.

2
00:00:08,353 --> 00:00:09,617
It often works.

3
00:00:09,617 --> 00:00:13,031
But if it does not work for you, do not stop there.

4
00:00:13,031 --> 00:00:17,021
You register on Bima Bharosa, upload your papers, and wait.

5
00:00:17,021 --> 00:00:22,870
Many people then get the same rejection letter from the insurance company again, and the complaint is closed.

6
00:00:22,870 --> 00:00:26,619
And you think, even the government portal could not help me.

7
00:00:26,619 --> 00:00:27,604
Here is why.

8
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:29,602
Bima Bharosa is useful.

9
00:00:29,602 --> 00:00:34,216
Your complaint goes on the regulator's record, and the company has to answer it.

10
00:00:34,216 --> 00:00:37,202
But Bima Bharosa is NOT a court.

11
00:00:37,202 --> 00:00:44,466
Your complaint goes to the same insurance company that cut your claim, and the I-R-D-A-I tracks how the company handles it.

12
00:00:44,466 --> 00:00:50,222
Bima Bharosa does not decide your claim, and it does not pass an order telling the company to pay you.

13
00:00:50,222 --> 00:00:52,623
That is why step four exists.

14
00:00:52,623 --> 00:01:01,509
The body that can pass a binding award in your case... is the Insurance Ombudsman, which works under the Insurance Ombudsman Rules, twenty seventeen.

15
00:01:01,509 --> 00:01:03,434
Now, back to the second door.

16
00:01:03,434 --> 00:01:05,589
Private claim recovery companies.

17
00:01:05,589 --> 00:01:08,726
Suppose your three lakh thirty thousand rupees is stuck.

18
00:01:08,726 --> 00:01:15,528
A recovery agency tells you, sign our agreement, and if we get your money back, give us twenty percent plus G-S-T.

19
00:01:15,528 --> 00:01:19,737
Twenty percent of three lakh thirty thousand is sixty-six thousand rupees.

20
00:01:19,737 --> 00:01:27,263
Add eighteen percent G-S-T, and it is seventy-seven thousand eight hundred and eighty rupees out of your family's medical savings.

21
00:01:27,263 --> 00:01:29,698
And here is what they may not tell you.

22
00:01:29,698 --> 00:01:39,415
Under Rule fourteen of the Insurance Ombudsman Rules, the complaint is made by you, the person with the grievance, or through your legal heir, nominee or assignee.

23
00:01:39,415 --> 00:01:44,289
The form is the same free form on the official website that you can fill in yourself.

24
00:01:44,289 --> 00:01:47,996
And never share your passwords or O-T-Ps with anyone.

25
00:01:47,996 --> 00:01:52,789
So before you sign any agreement and give away a share of your money, remember.

26
00:01:52,789 --> 00:01:56,503
You can do this yourself online, for zero rupees.

27
00:01:56,503 --> 00:01:58,101
Now listen carefully.

28
00:01:58,101 --> 00:02:02,568
You cannot jump straight to the Ombudsman on the day your claim is rejected.

29
00:02:02,568 --> 00:02:06,253
If you do, your complaint can be turned away at the door.

30
00:02:06,253 --> 00:02:13,747
In twenty twenty-four to twenty-five alone, seventeen hundred and fifteen health complaints were turned away for this one reason.

31
00:02:13,747 --> 00:02:17,418
The person had not complained to the insurance company first.

32
00:02:17,418 --> 00:02:21,203
Under Rule fourteen, you must follow a two-step clock.

33
00:02:21,203 --> 00:02:22,601
Clock step one.

34
00:02:22,601 --> 00:02:24,803
This is step two of our plan.

35
00:02:24,803 --> 00:02:31,951
Complain in writing to the insurance company, best of all to its Grievance Redressal Officer, the G-R-O.

36
00:02:31,951 --> 00:02:39,814
Every insurer has to show its grievance officer's details on its website, and the Ombudsman's website lists their email addresses too.

37
00:02:39,814 --> 00:02:46,869
Send one calm, formal email with your policy number, your claim number, and why their deduction is wrong.

38
00:02:46,869 --> 00:02:49,785
Keep a copy of that email and every reply.

39
00:02:49,785 --> 00:02:51,213
You will need them later.

40
00:02:51,213 --> 00:02:57,201
Under the I-R-D-A-I rules, the company should resolve your grievance within fourteen days.

41
00:02:57,201 --> 00:02:58,612
Clock step two.

42
00:02:58,612 --> 00:03:01,814
Wait for their reply, or wait one month.

43
00:03:01,814 --> 00:03:12,337
The moment the company rejects your complaint, or you are not happy with its reply, or one month passes with no reply at all... the door to the Ombudsman opens.

44
00:03:12,337 --> 00:03:19,549
From that day, you have one year to file your complaint with the Ombudsman, for compensation of up to fifty lakh rupees.

45
00:03:19,549 --> 00:03:23,738
That limit was raised to fifty lakh rupees in November twenty twenty-three.

46
00:03:23,738 --> 00:03:25,995
And remember one strict condition.

47
00:03:25,995 --> 00:03:35,842
The Ombudsman cannot take your complaint if the same dispute is already pending, or already decided, in any court, consumer forum, or arbitration.

48
00:03:35,842 --> 00:03:39,657
So, how do you actually file, and what happens next?

49
00:03:39,657 --> 00:03:44,780
Open your browser and go to the official website, c-i-o-i-n-s dot co dot in.

50
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:50,580
Choose Register Complaint, and verify your mobile number with an O-T-P.

51
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:53,003
Then you choose your Ombudsman office.

52
00:03:53,003 --> 00:04:00,031
There are eighteen offices across India, in cities like Hyderabad, Bengaluru, Mumbai, Delhi and Kolkata.

53
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:06,028
You pick the one that covers the place where you live, or the insurance company's branch that handled your policy.

54
00:04:06,028 --> 00:04:08,887
Before you submit, keep these documents ready.

55
00:04:08,887 --> 00:04:09,498
One.

56
00:04:09,498 --> 00:04:11,710
A copy of your insurance policy.

57
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:12,274
Two.

58
00:04:12,274 --> 00:04:15,871
The hospital discharge summary and the itemised final bill.

59
00:04:15,871 --> 00:04:16,472
Three.

60
00:04:16,472 --> 00:04:19,308
The company's rejection or deduction letter.

61
00:04:19,308 --> 00:04:19,922
Four.

62
00:04:19,922 --> 00:04:23,134
A copy of the complaint you sent to the insurance company.

63
00:04:23,134 --> 00:04:24,026
And five.

64
00:04:24,026 --> 00:04:27,180
Your I-D and address proof, and a photograph.

65
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:31,212
Each file can be a P-D-F or a J-P-G, up to ten M-B.

66
00:04:31,212 --> 00:04:34,839
Check every detail, tick the declaration, and submit.

67
00:04:34,839 --> 00:04:38,178
Your complaint is verified first, and then registered.

68
00:04:38,178 --> 00:04:40,946
Save the acknowledgement and your complaint number.

69
00:04:40,946 --> 00:04:42,696
Now, what happens next?

70
00:04:42,696 --> 00:04:46,358
The Ombudsman hears both sides, you and the company.

71
00:04:46,358 --> 00:04:49,590
The hearing can be in person, or online by video.

72
00:04:49,590 --> 00:04:53,035
Many complaints end in mediation under Rule sixteen.

73
00:04:53,035 --> 00:04:58,135
The Ombudsman suggests a fair settlement, and if both sides agree, the case closes.

74
00:04:58,135 --> 00:05:04,339
In twenty twenty-four to twenty-five, about one in three health complaints that were closed, ended this way.

75
00:05:04,339 --> 00:05:08,999
If there is no settlement, the Ombudsman decides the case, and passes an award.

76
00:05:08,999 --> 00:05:11,073
You don't need fancy legal words.

77
00:05:11,073 --> 00:05:13,018
Explain your case simply.

78
00:05:13,018 --> 00:05:14,576
When did you buy the policy?

79
00:05:14,576 --> 00:05:16,061
Why were you in the hospital?

80
00:05:16,061 --> 00:05:18,060
And how much did the company cut?

81
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,856
And how long does it take?

82
00:05:19,856 --> 00:05:27,502
Of the health complaints the Ombudsman closed in twenty twenty-four to twenty-five, about eight out of ten were closed within three months.

83
00:05:27,502 --> 00:05:30,445
And here is why this law is built for you.

84
00:05:30,445 --> 00:05:31,165
First.

85
00:05:31,165 --> 00:05:36,929
Under Rule seventeen, when the Ombudsman passes an award, it is binding on the insurance company.

86
00:05:36,929 --> 00:05:39,720
Wait... what if you are NOT happy with the award?

87
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,378
You don't have to accept it.

88
00:05:41,378 --> 00:05:45,296
Other legal remedies, like the consumer forum, may still be open to you.

89
00:05:45,296 --> 00:05:46,251
And second.

90
00:05:46,251 --> 00:05:55,413
Under the I-R-D-A-I health master circular of twenty twenty-four, the insurance company must carry out the award within thirty days of receiving it.

91
00:05:55,413 --> 00:06:06,041
If it is late, and it has not challenged the award within those thirty days, it must pay you a penalty of five thousand rupees for every day of delay, on top of any interest that is due.

92
00:06:06,041 --> 00:06:09,040
Ten days late, that is fifty thousand rupees.

93
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:12,603
Thirty days late, one lakh fifty thousand rupees.

94
00:06:12,603 --> 00:06:22,516
And in December twenty twenty-four, the Bombay High Court heard the case of a senior citizen who had won an Ombudsman award, but was not paid for more than three years.

95
00:06:22,516 --> 00:06:35,426
The court ordered the insurance company to pay the award with interest, plus one lakh rupees in costs, and said the costs and interest should be recovered from the officers responsible, after an inquiry.

96
00:06:35,426 --> 00:06:38,193
That is the power of knowing your rights.

97
00:06:38,193 --> 00:06:42,547
You don't need connections, and you don't need to pay twenty percent to middlemen.

98
00:06:42,547 --> 00:06:43,565
Be smart.

99
00:06:43,565 --> 00:06:44,871
Be informed.

100
00:06:44,871 --> 00:06:47,343
And always... be practical.

101
00:06:47,343 --> 00:06:53,236
In our next episode, we look at consumables, the gloves, masks and syringes on your bill.

102
00:06:53,236 --> 00:07:02,321
We will open a five lakh rupee hospital bill, line by line, look at what we pay for these consumables, and what the government's price rules say about them.

103
00:07:02,321 --> 00:07:07,063
Hit the subscribe button, share this video with your family, and drop your questions below.

104
00:07:07,063 --> 00:07:08,748
I'll see you in the next video.

